(Supported by NRTA's Online Audiovisual
Quality Creation & Distribution Project)

2
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:29,530
♪Black hair twines around bone♪

3
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:35,360
♪Night dew cold♪

4
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:39,750
♪Bronze mirror cracks
through three lifetimes♪

5
00:00:40,490 --> 00:00:44,040
♪Shines on the sleepless♪

6
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:48,580
♪Yunmeng Marsh ebbs and flows♪

7
00:00:49,050 --> 00:00:52,730
♪Vows sink deep♪

8
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:58,360
♪White-hair curse turns to snow♪

9
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:03,170
♪Covering the realm♪

10
00:01:07,530 --> 00:01:11,020
=Reunion Across Time=

11
00:01:11,050 --> 00:01:14,080
=Episode 2=

12
00:01:16,056 --> 00:01:17,110
(Shaman Clan Register)

13
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:29,480
What's wrong?

14
00:01:30,959 --> 00:01:31,599
I can't read.

15
00:01:31,599 --> 00:01:32,103
(Shaman Clan Register)

16
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:36,000
So what if I can't read?

17
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:37,719
I grew up in the Shaman Clan.

18
00:01:37,879 --> 00:01:39,120
Of course I only know
Shaman Clan script.

19
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:40,079
What's so funny?

20
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:46,280
(What a loving couple.)

21
00:01:47,879 --> 00:01:50,640
(Why must they be torn apart?)

22
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:58,560
She's your sweetheart?

23
00:01:59,959 --> 00:02:01,000
I don't have a sweetheart.

24
00:02:01,959 --> 00:02:03,040
What did she just say?

25
00:02:03,159 --> 00:02:04,239
"Tear them apart"?

26
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,519
You let that girl down.

27
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:08,400
I didn't.

28
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:10,120
What a jerk.

29
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,599
Why is heaven so unfair to me,

30
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,520
making me watch others

31
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:16,960
be all lovey-dovey?

32
00:02:17,319 --> 00:02:18,400
We're not!

33
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:22,680
If that's the case,

34
00:02:23,039 --> 00:02:24,159
I'll just have to

35
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,560
kill you.

36
00:02:27,439 --> 00:02:28,840
What does that have to do with me?

37
00:02:29,159 --> 00:02:29,960
How vulgar.

38
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:34,680
So you're a shamaness.

39
00:02:35,159 --> 00:02:37,639
It seems you can bear
my primordial spirit.

40
00:02:37,879 --> 00:02:38,960
Come with me.

41
00:02:59,479 --> 00:03:01,360
(If you want to save your lover,)

42
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:03,360
(come find me.)

43
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:05,840
My Grand Shaman ambitions...

44
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:14,360
Song Ziyuan.

45
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:15,120
Don't come closer.

46
00:03:16,639 --> 00:03:18,000
For your lover,

47
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:19,639
you'd brave danger all alone.

48
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:22,000
How touching.

49
00:03:22,599 --> 00:03:23,960
Are lovers

50
00:03:24,159 --> 00:03:25,360
all you ever think about?

51
00:03:29,159 --> 00:03:30,080
Moonflower?

52
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:31,479
No wonder.

53
00:03:32,479 --> 00:03:33,680
I heard your kind

54
00:03:33,919 --> 00:03:35,479
must cling to trees to grow.

55
00:03:35,919 --> 00:03:37,400
Your kind falls hardest in love.

56
00:03:38,639 --> 00:03:40,080
But my beloved locust tree's body

57
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:42,039
is already dead.

58
00:03:42,479 --> 00:03:45,159
Plants like us have fragile bodies.

59
00:03:45,599 --> 00:03:47,759
If we had human bodies,

60
00:03:48,039 --> 00:03:49,680
we wouldn't die so easily.

61
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:50,879
So,

62
00:03:51,039 --> 00:03:52,639
let me have your body.

63
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,319
So it was you

64
00:03:57,719 --> 00:03:58,800
searching the city all along

65
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:00,080
for a body to house your spirit.

66
00:04:00,599 --> 00:04:01,319
That's why those people

67
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,599
couldn't bear your spirit

68
00:04:02,879 --> 00:04:03,680
and mutated and died.

69
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,159
They were ordinary people.

70
00:04:06,479 --> 00:04:07,560
But you're different.

71
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:08,919
You're a shamaness.

72
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:10,360
You can do it.

73
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:12,240
Let him down now!

74
00:04:13,759 --> 00:04:14,319
No.

75
00:04:15,039 --> 00:04:17,079
He'll soon be my beloved locust tree.

76
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:29,879
Your blood can hurt her.

77
00:04:40,519 --> 00:04:41,959
How did you know
my blood could hurt her?

78
00:04:42,279 --> 00:04:44,279
Your blood can actually hurt me?

79
00:04:44,639 --> 00:04:46,079
Impressive.

80
00:04:51,959 --> 00:04:52,560
Help me!

81
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:36,079
My beloved locust tree,

82
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,879
As you live, I live.

83
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:42,279
If you die, I'll follow.

84
00:05:43,399 --> 00:05:44,519
My beloved locust tree...

85
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:05,480
Song Ziyuan,

86
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,560
why did you save me?

87
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,399
Weren't you going to kill me?

88
00:06:10,399 --> 00:06:11,959
How did you know
my blood could hurt her?

89
00:06:13,199 --> 00:06:14,199
Tell me!

90
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:17,839
I never thought...

91
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,079
the last time...

92
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:23,040
would end like this...

93
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:24,319
I...

94
00:06:24,439 --> 00:06:25,199
Song Ziyuan,

95
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:26,319
what do you mean, last time?

96
00:06:28,079 --> 00:06:28,720
You...

97
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:31,800
Song Ziyuan!

98
00:06:32,439 --> 00:06:33,319
(Why?)

99
00:06:33,639 --> 00:06:35,079
(Why does my heart ache so much?)

100
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:45,040
What on earth is going on?

101
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:47,560
Song Ziyuan,

102
00:06:48,959 --> 00:06:49,879
who are you really?

103
00:07:07,319 --> 00:07:08,480
I need to know everything.

104
00:07:11,199 --> 00:07:12,319
I'm a shamaness.

105
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:14,480
I can call your soul back.

106
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:16,319
Song Ziyuan,

107
00:07:16,879 --> 00:07:17,920
I'm bringing you back to life.

108
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,720
(Scorching sun burns its feathers.)

109
00:07:36,639 --> 00:07:38,360
(Drifting sands bury the spirit altar.)

110
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:41,639
(Xuanming Soul-Freezing Banner.)

111
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:44,360
(Rivers chill the bones.)

112
00:07:48,279 --> 00:07:49,399
(Soul...)

113
00:07:51,199 --> 00:07:52,160
(Return!)

114
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:00,600
Song Ziyuan, wake up.

115
00:08:01,399 --> 00:08:02,079
Wake up.

116
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:14,800
No.

117
00:08:17,279 --> 00:08:18,000
Something's wrong.

118
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:19,439
How can this be?

119
00:08:20,879 --> 00:08:22,279
Everyone has
three souls and seven spirits.

120
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:24,240
Why do you only have
a wisp of your soul left?

121
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:27,480
There's no other way.

122
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:29,040
I'll have to use this.

123
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:39,480
I trade my soul

124
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,279
for the return of yours.

125
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,279
Didn't I die?

126
00:09:12,399 --> 00:09:13,000
This is...

127
00:09:14,399 --> 00:09:15,600
It's my corpse.

128
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:17,559
Then I'm...

129
00:09:18,559 --> 00:09:19,639
a spirit now?

130
00:09:23,759 --> 00:09:24,480
Could it be

131
00:09:25,519 --> 00:09:26,720
that Chu Li and I...

132
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:36,080
We did it.

133
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:37,879
You're

134
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:39,320
Chu Li?

135
00:09:40,399 --> 00:09:41,399
You're

136
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:42,960
Song Ziyuan now?

137
00:09:48,737 --> 00:09:55,487
♪Night rain falls in the courtyard,
shining on mortal partings♪

138
00:09:55,897 --> 00:10:02,567
♪Strangers meet again,
past lives gleam in endless hues♪

139
00:10:02,937 --> 00:10:06,257
♪A sharp arrow pierces memory♪

140
00:10:06,427 --> 00:10:09,627
♪Longing spreads like dye♪

141
00:10:09,957 --> 00:10:16,617
♪Beaded curtains
keep love and hate apart♪

142
00:10:17,037 --> 00:10:23,697
♪Through boundless grief,
love remains hard to sever♪

143
00:10:23,987 --> 00:10:30,347
♪A past bond, a parting dream;
when cold ends, purest joy remains♪

144
00:10:30,517 --> 00:10:33,947
♪That year,
pear blossoms, verse, and laughter♪

145
00:10:34,207 --> 00:10:37,427
♪One night, snow fell in wild flurries♪

146
00:10:37,467 --> 00:10:44,347
♪All perfection in this world
hides regret♪

147
00:10:44,697 --> 00:10:48,227
♪A drop of heart's blood seals love♪

148
00:10:48,387 --> 00:10:51,947
♪No more longing enters dreams♪

149
00:10:52,347 --> 00:10:58,787
♪When all turns to mist,
may you and I be safe forever♪

150
00:11:27,697 --> 00:11:34,367
♪Through boundless grief,
love remains hard to sever♪

151
00:11:34,617 --> 00:11:40,907
♪A past bond, a parting dream;
when cold ends, purest joy remains♪
